# Harness output. bootqa.mjs writes a screenshot of the title screen every run;
# it is evidence for the run that produced it, not a tracked asset.
bootqa-*.png

# The per-mode screenshots bootqa writes now that it walks the lobby, and the
# look-capture sets lookqa.mjs writes per tag. Same argument as above and a
# sharper one: a tagged capture set is nine PNGs PER RUN, and the whole point of
# the harness is that you take a `before` and an `after` every time you touch
# the palette. Tracked, that is a repo that grows without bound with images
# nobody will ever open twice.
shots/
